cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "primus-paleo: simulation and track-identification framework for cosmic-ray paleo-detectors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/cgalelli/primus-paleo"
abstract: >-
  Code for the PRImuS paleo-detector project: simulation of nuclear-recoil
  track spectra in minerals from past cosmic-ray fluxes (mineral_utils,
  flux_history; MCEq, and Geant4 inputs), the OptimusPrimus deep-learning
  pipeline for track identification in optical microscopy images, and the notebooks
  reproducing the figures of the associated analyses. Simulation outputs are not
  included but can be regenerated with the provided code.
keywords:
  - paleo-detectors
  - cosmic rays
  - nuclear recoil tracks
  - Geant4
  - deep learning
  - track detection
authors:
  - family-names: Galelli
    given-names: Claudio
    email: claudio.galelli@mi.infn.it
    affiliation: "INFN, Sezione di Milano"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7372-9703"
  
